IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-interpretation`
IMPORT `g1-art1-defined-terms`
IMPORT `g1-art2-entity`
IMPORT `g1-art2-governor-misconduct`

-- g1-tests-art2-governor-misconduct.l4: tests of Article 2(7) to (10), with every expected value decided from the source before the module was run.

§ `Part 1 — Interpretation: tests of Article 2(7) to (10)`

§§ `2(7) to (9): governor`

-- The people. Each is described by the roles the person holds.
`a trustee` MEANS
    `Facts about a person's role in an entity` WITH
        `a trustee of the trust or a fidéicommissaire of the fidéicommis` IS TRUE
        `a member of the council of the foundation` IS FALSE
        `a director of the company` IS FALSE
        `a member of the management committee of the entity` IS FALSE
        `relation to the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` IS `holds none of the general control and management`

`a council member` MEANS
    `Facts about a person's role in an entity` WITH
        `a trustee of the trust or a fidéicommissaire of the fidéicommis` IS FALSE
        `a member of the council of the foundation` IS TRUE
        `a director of the company` IS FALSE
        `a member of the management committee of the entity` IS FALSE
        `relation to the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` IS `holds none of the general control and management`

`a director` MEANS
    `Facts about a person's role in an entity` WITH
        `a trustee of the trust or a fidéicommissaire of the fidéicommis` IS FALSE
        `a member of the council of the foundation` IS FALSE
        `a director of the company` IS TRUE
        `a member of the management committee of the entity` IS FALSE
        `relation to the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` IS `holds none of the general control and management`

`a committee member` MEANS
    `Facts about a person's role in an entity` WITH
        `a trustee of the trust or a fidéicommissaire of the fidéicommis` IS FALSE
        `a member of the council of the foundation` IS FALSE
        `a director of the company` IS FALSE
        `a member of the management committee of the entity` IS TRUE
        `relation to the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` IS `holds none of the general control and management`

GIVEN relation IS A `Relation to the general control and management`
GIVETH A `Facts about a person's role in an entity`
`a person with no office who` relation MEANS
    `Facts about a person's role in an entity` WITH
        `a trustee of the trust or a fidéicommissaire of the fidéicommis` IS FALSE
        `a member of the council of the foundation` IS FALSE
        `a director of the company` IS FALSE
        `a member of the management committee of the entity` IS FALSE
        `relation to the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` IS relation

`a person with the control alone` MEANS `a person with no office who` `holds the general control and management alone`
`a person with the control as one of a number` MEANS `a person with no office who` `holds the general control and management as one of a number of governors`
`an agent of the person with the control` MEANS `a person with no office who` `exercises the general control and management only on behalf of another who holds it in that other's own right`
`a stranger` MEANS `a person with no office who` `holds none of the general control and management`

-- A trustee who is also a director, as a corporate trustee's officer might be: both roles.
`a trustee who is also a director` MEANS
    `Facts about a person's role in an entity` WITH
        `a trustee of the trust or a fidéicommissaire of the fidéicommis` IS TRUE
        `a member of the council of the foundation` IS FALSE
        `a director of the company` IS TRUE
        `a member of the management committee of the entity` IS FALSE
        `relation to the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` IS `holds none of the general control and management`

-- The model constitution of Article 2(8).
`no model` MEANS
    `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)` WITH
        `the constitution conforms to the model` IS FALSE
        `published by the Commissioner` IS `Facts about a publication` WITH
            `made available by the person in some manner` IS FALSE
            `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS FALSE
            `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS FALSE
        `published for the purpose of Article 2(8)` IS FALSE
        `the model provides for the entity to have a management committee` IS FALSE

`a relevant model` MEANS
    `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)` WITH
        `the constitution conforms to the model` IS TRUE
        `published by the Commissioner` IS `Facts about a publication` WITH
            `made available by the person in some manner` IS TRUE
            `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE
            `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE
        `published for the purpose of Article 2(8)` IS TRUE
        `the model provides for the entity to have a management committee` IS TRUE

-- The discriminating case of F1.5 inside Article 2(8)(b)(i): the Commissioner posted the model where nobody would see it, and honestly thinks that enough.
`a model in a locked cabinet` MEANS
    `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)` WITH
        `the constitution conforms to the model` IS TRUE
        `published by the Commissioner` IS `Facts about a publication` WITH
            `made available by the person in some manner` IS TRUE
            `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE
            `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS FALSE
        `published for the purpose of Article 2(8)` IS TRUE
        `the model provides for the entity to have a management committee` IS TRUE

`a model that does not conform` MEANS
    `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)` WITH
        `the constitution conforms to the model` IS FALSE
        `published by the Commissioner` IS `Facts about a publication` WITH
            `made available by the person in some manner` IS TRUE
            `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE
            `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE
        `published for the purpose of Article 2(8)` IS TRUE
        `the model provides for the entity to have a management committee` IS TRUE

`a model never made available` MEANS
    `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)` WITH
        `the constitution conforms to the model` IS TRUE
        `published by the Commissioner` IS `Facts about a publication` WITH
            `made available by the person in some manner` IS FALSE
            `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE
            `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE
        `published for the purpose of Article 2(8)` IS TRUE
        `the model provides for the entity to have a management committee` IS TRUE

`a model not published for the purpose` MEANS
    `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)` WITH
        `the constitution conforms to the model` IS TRUE
        `published by the Commissioner` IS `Facts about a publication` WITH
            `made available by the person in some manner` IS TRUE
            `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE
            `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE
        `published for the purpose of Article 2(8)` IS FALSE
        `the model provides for the entity to have a management committee` IS TRUE

`a model with no management committee` MEANS
    `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)` WITH
        `the constitution conforms to the model` IS TRUE
        `published by the Commissioner` IS `Facts about a publication` WITH
            `made available by the person in some manner` IS TRUE
            `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE
            `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE
        `published for the purpose of Article 2(8)` IS TRUE
        `the model provides for the entity to have a management committee` IS FALSE

-- The kinds, as short names.
`kinds: trust` MEANS LIST `the trustees of a trust`
`kinds: fidéicommis` MEANS LIST `the fidéicommissaires of a court-approved fidéicommis`
`kinds: foundation` MEANS LIST `a foundation`
`kinds: company` MEANS LIST `a company`
`kinds: unincorporated body` MEANS LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`
`kinds: NPO body corporate` MEANS LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`
`kinds: 1862 association` MEANS LIST `an incorporated 1862 association`
`kinds: statutory body` MEANS LIST `a body corporate established by an enactment, an Act of the States or a Royal Charter`
`kinds: body within (g)` MEANS LIST `a body incorporated under, but not by, an enactment other than the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
`kinds: body within (h)` MEANS LIST `a body incorporated under, but not by, an Act of the United Kingdom Parliament or Order in Council`
`kinds: foreign analogue` MEANS LIST `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction`
`kinds: body added by an Order` MEANS LIST (`an entity added by an Order under Article 2(2)` "(k)")
`kinds: company that is the sole trustee` MEANS LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a company`
`kinds: foundation that is the sole trustee` MEANS LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a foundation`
`kinds: NPO body corporate that is the sole trustee` MEANS LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`
`kinds: unincorporated body that is the sole trustee` MEANS LIST `the trustees of a trust`, `an unincorporated body or association of persons`
`kinds: foundation and company` MEANS LIST `a foundation`, `a company`
`no kind` MEANS EMPTY

GIVEN kinds IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
      person IS A `Facts about a person's role in an entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` kinds `the person` person MEANS
    `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` kinds `no model` person

-- (a): a trust or fidéicommis: a trustee or fidéicommissaire. Nobody else, whatever else they have.
#ASSERT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: trust` `the person` `a trustee`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: trust` `the person` `a director`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: trust` `the person` `a council member`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: trust` `the person` `a committee member`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: trust` `the person` `a person with the control alone`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: trust` `the person` `a stranger`
#ASSERT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: fidéicommis` `the person` `a trustee`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: fidéicommis` `the person` `a director`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: fidéicommis` `the person` `a person with the control alone`

-- (b): a foundation: a member of the council.
#ASSERT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: foundation` `the person` `a council member`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: foundation` `the person` `a trustee`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: foundation` `the person` `a director`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: foundation` `the person` `a person with the control alone`

-- (c): a company: a director.
#ASSERT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: company` `the person` `a director`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: company` `the person` `a trustee`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: company` `the person` `a council member`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: company` `the person` `a person with the control alone`

-- (e): in any other case, a person who under the constitution has the general control and management of the administration of the entity.
#ASSERT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: NPO body corporate` `the person` `a person with the control alone`
#ASSERT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: 1862 association` `the person` `a person with the control alone`
#ASSERT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: statutory body` `the person` `a person with the control alone`
#ASSERT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: body within (g)` `the person` `a person with the control alone`
#ASSERT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: body within (h)` `the person` `a person with the control alone`
#ASSERT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: foreign analogue` `the person` `a person with the control alone`
#ASSERT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: body added by an Order` `the person` `a person with the control alone`
#ASSERT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: unincorporated body` `the person` `a person with the control alone`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: NPO body corporate` `the person` `a trustee`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: NPO body corporate` `the person` `a director`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: NPO body corporate` `the person` `a committee member`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: NPO body corporate` `the person` `a stranger`

-- Article 2(9)(b): alone or as one of a number of governors; Article 2(9)(a): not merely by exercising it on behalf of another who has it in that other's own right.
#ASSERT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: NPO body corporate` `the person` `a person with the control as one of a number`
#ASSERT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: unincorporated body` `the person` `a person with the control as one of a number`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: NPO body corporate` `the person` `an agent of the person with the control`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `kinds: unincorporated body` `the person` `an agent of the person with the control`
#ASSERT `Art 2(9)(b) the person has the general control and management alone or as one of a number of governors` `a person with the control alone`
#ASSERT `Art 2(9)(b) the person has the general control and management alone or as one of a number of governors` `a person with the control as one of a number`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(b) the person has the general control and management alone or as one of a number of governors` `an agent of the person with the control`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(b) the person has the general control and management alone or as one of a number of governors` `a stranger`
#ASSERT `Art 2(9)(a) the person only exercises the general control and management on behalf of another who has it in own right` `an agent of the person with the control`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(a) the person only exercises the general control and management on behalf of another who has it in own right` `a person with the control alone`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(9)(a) the person only exercises the general control and management on behalf of another who has it in own right` `a stranger`
#ASSERT `Art 2(7)(e) the person has the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` `a person with the control alone`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7)(e) the person has the general control and management of the administration of the entity under its constitution` `an agent of the person with the control`

-- Not an entity: nobody is a governor of it.
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `no kind` `the person` `a person with the control alone`
#ASSERT NOT `governor, in the favoured reading, with no model:` `no kind` `the person` `a director`

§§ `2(8) relevant unincorporated entity, and (7)(d)`

GIVEN kinds IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
      model IS A `Facts about the model constitution of Article 2(8)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`relevant unincorporated entity, in the favoured reading:` kinds `with the model` model MEANS
    `Art 2(8) the entity is a relevant unincorporated entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` kinds model

#ASSERT `relevant unincorporated entity, in the favoured reading:` `kinds: unincorporated body` `with the model` `a relevant model`
#ASSERT NOT `relevant unincorporated entity, in the favoured reading:` `kinds: company` `with the model` `a relevant model`
#ASSERT NOT `relevant unincorporated entity, in the favoured reading:` `kinds: unincorporated body` `with the model` `no model`
#ASSERT NOT `relevant unincorporated entity, in the favoured reading:` `kinds: unincorporated body` `with the model` `a model that does not conform`
#ASSERT NOT `relevant unincorporated entity, in the favoured reading:` `kinds: unincorporated body` `with the model` `a model never made available`
#ASSERT NOT `relevant unincorporated entity, in the favoured reading:` `kinds: unincorporated body` `with the model` `a model not published for the purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `relevant unincorporated entity, in the favoured reading:` `kinds: unincorporated body` `with the model` `a model with no management committee`
#ASSERT NOT `relevant unincorporated entity, in the favoured reading:` `no kind` `with the model` `a relevant model`

-- F1.5 inside (8)(b)(i): the model in the locked cabinet is published on the Commissioner's opinion, and not on the likelihood of the manner.
#ASSERT `relevant unincorporated entity, in the favoured reading:` `kinds: unincorporated body` `with the model` `a model in a locked cabinet`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(8) the entity is a relevant unincorporated entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.5 read the other way` `kinds: unincorporated body` `a model in a locked cabinet`
#ASSERT `Art 2(8) the entity is a relevant unincorporated entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.5 read the other way` `kinds: unincorporated body` `a relevant model`

-- (7)(d): a relevant unincorporated entity: a member of the management committee, and not a person with the control as such.
#ASSERT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `kinds: unincorporated body` `a relevant model` `a committee member`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `kinds: unincorporated body` `a relevant model` `a person with the control alone`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `kinds: unincorporated body` `a relevant model` `a director`
-- ... and an unincorporated body that is not a relevant unincorporated entity falls under (e): the person with the control, and not the committee member as such.
#ASSERT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `kinds: unincorporated body` `a model that does not conform` `a person with the control alone`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `kinds: unincorporated body` `a model that does not conform` `a committee member`
-- F1.5 at (7): the locked-cabinet model makes the body a relevant unincorporated entity on reading A, so the committee member is a governor; on reading B it falls under (e).
#ASSERT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `kinds: unincorporated body` `a model in a locked cabinet` `a committee member`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `kinds: unincorporated body` `a model in a locked cabinet` `a person with the control alone`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.5 read the other way` `kinds: unincorporated body` `a model in a locked cabinet` `a committee member`
#ASSERT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.5 read the other way` `kinds: unincorporated body` `a model in a locked cabinet` `a person with the control alone`

§§ `2(7): a body in more than one kind (fork F1.4)`

-- A company that is the sole trustee is a trust (a) and a company (c) (Article 8(3)(a)(i)).
-- Reading A (taken): every case that applies: the trustee and the company's director are both governors. Reading B: the first case, (a): the trustee only.
#ASSERT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `kinds: company that is the sole trustee` `no model` `a trustee`
#ASSERT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `kinds: company that is the sole trustee` `no model` `a director`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `kinds: company that is the sole trustee` `no model` `a stranger`
#ASSERT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` `kinds: company that is the sole trustee` `no model` `a trustee`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` `kinds: company that is the sole trustee` `no model` `a director`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` `kinds: company that is the sole trustee` `no model` `a stranger`
-- A person who is both: governor on either reading.
#ASSERT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` `kinds: company that is the sole trustee` `no model` `a trustee who is also a director`
-- A foundation that is the sole trustee: the council member is a governor on reading A, and on reading B only the trustee.
#ASSERT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `kinds: foundation that is the sole trustee` `no model` `a council member`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` `kinds: foundation that is the sole trustee` `no model` `a council member`
-- The paragraph's order, not the kinds' order: a foundation (b) and a company (c): on reading B the council member, not the director.
#ASSERT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` `kinds: foundation and company` `no model` `a council member`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` `kinds: foundation and company` `no model` `a director`
#ASSERT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `kinds: foundation and company` `no model` `a director`
-- (e), "in any other case", applies only when none of (a) to (d) does: an NPO body corporate that is the sole trustee has trustees as governors, and not also a person with the control.
#ASSERT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `kinds: NPO body corporate that is the sole trustee` `no model` `a trustee`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `kinds: NPO body corporate that is the sole trustee` `no model` `a person with the control alone`
-- An unincorporated body that is the sole trustee, with a relevant model: trustee (a) and committee member (d) on reading A; the trustee only on reading B.
#ASSERT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `kinds: unincorporated body that is the sole trustee` `a relevant model` `a committee member`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` `kinds: unincorporated body that is the sole trustee` `a relevant model` `a committee member`
#ASSERT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` `kinds: unincorporated body that is the sole trustee` `a relevant model` `a trustee`
-- A single kind gives the same answer on both readings.
#ASSERT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` `kinds: company` `no model` `a director`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(7) the person is a governor of the entity` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` `kinds: company` `no model` `a trustee`

§§ `2(7): the governors among the people`

`Mr Alpha, a director` MEANS
    `Person considered as a governor` WITH
        person IS Governor WITH
            name IS "Mr Alpha"
            `is a natural person` IS TRUE
            `is resident in Jersey` IS TRUE
            `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS FALSE
            `reportable matters` IS EMPTY
        role IS `a director`
`Ms Beta, a stranger` MEANS
    `Person considered as a governor` WITH
        person IS Governor WITH
            name IS "Ms Beta"
            `is a natural person` IS TRUE
            `is resident in Jersey` IS FALSE
            `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS FALSE
            `reportable matters` IS EMPTY
        role IS `a stranger`
`Gamma Limited, a trustee` MEANS
    `Person considered as a governor` WITH
        person IS Governor WITH
            name IS "Gamma Limited"
            `is a natural person` IS FALSE
            `is resident in Jersey` IS FALSE
            `is itself a Jersey entity by virtue of Article 2(3)(a)` IS TRUE
            `reportable matters` IS EMPTY
        role IS `a trustee`

#ASSERT map (GIVEN governor YIELD governor's name) (`Art 2(7) the governors among the people` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `kinds: company that is the sole trustee` `no model` (LIST `Mr Alpha, a director`, `Ms Beta, a stranger`, `Gamma Limited, a trustee`)) EQUALS LIST "Mr Alpha", "Gamma Limited"
#ASSERT map (GIVEN governor YIELD governor's name) (`Art 2(7) the governors among the people` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.4 read the other way` `kinds: company that is the sole trustee` `no model` (LIST `Mr Alpha, a director`, `Ms Beta, a stranger`, `Gamma Limited, a trustee`)) EQUALS LIST "Gamma Limited"
#ASSERT map (GIVEN governor YIELD governor's name) (`Art 2(7) the governors among the people` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `no kind` `no model` (LIST `Mr Alpha, a director`)) EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `2(10): misconduct`

-- Test-only: the statements true of a piece of conduct, as in the tests of Article 2(1).
DECLARE `A thing true of the conduct` IS ONE OF
    `it is by the registered charity or by one of its governors`
    `it contravenes the constitution`
    `it contravenes the constitutional Law`
    `it contravenes a required steps notice`
    `it contravenes a court order under this Law`
    `it contravenes a court order under an enactment under this Law`
    `it contravenes a court order under the constitutional Law`
    `it contravenes a court order under an enactment under the constitutional Law`
    `it is an offence in relation to the entity`
    `it is an offence under the constitutional Law of that charity or other entity`
    `it is an offence under the financial services Laws`
    `it is an offence under the tax Laws`
    `it is an offence relating to money laundering or terrorist financing`
    `it is an offence involving deception or dishonesty`
    `it is an offence under foreign law similar to those`
    `the entity is equivalent to a registered charity abroad`

GIVEN true IS A LIST OF `A thing true of the conduct`
      then IS A `Standing on the register`
      now IS A `Standing on the register`
      laws IS A LIST OF `Constitutional Law of an entity`
GIVETH A `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)`
`a piece of conduct of which` true `is true, with the entity` then `at the time and` now `when asked, and the laws` laws MEANS
    `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)` WITH
        `standing of the entity when the conduct occurred` IS then
        `standing of the entity when the question is asked` IS now
        `the constitutional Laws of the charity` IS laws
        `an entity equivalent to a registered charity under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey` IS elem `the entity is equivalent to a registered charity abroad` true
        `by the registered charity or by one of its governors` IS elem `it is by the registered charity or by one of its governors` true
        `a contravention of a provision of the constitution of the registered charity` IS elem `it contravenes the constitution` true
        `a contravention of a provision of the constitutional Law of the charity` IS elem `it contravenes the constitutional Law` true
        `a contravention of a provision of a required steps notice` IS elem `it contravenes a required steps notice` true
        `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under this Law` IS elem `it contravenes a court order under this Law` true
        `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under an enactment under this Law` IS elem `it contravenes a court order under an enactment under this Law` true
        `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under the constitutional Law of the charity` IS elem `it contravenes a court order under the constitutional Law` true
        `a contravention of a provision of an order of the court under an enactment under the constitutional Law of the charity` IS elem `it contravenes a court order under an enactment under the constitutional Law` true
        `the offence is in relation to the entity` IS elem `it is an offence in relation to the entity` true
        `an offence under the constitutional Law of that charity or other entity` IS elem `it is an offence under the constitutional Law of that charity or other entity` true
        `an offence under the financial services Laws, any Regulation or Order made under them, or the Alternative Investment Funds (Jersey) Regulations 2012` IS elem `it is an offence under the financial services Laws` true
        `an offence under the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961, the Goods and Services Tax (Jersey) Law 2007 or the Taxation (Land Transactions) (Jersey) Law 2009` IS elem `it is an offence under the tax Laws` true
        `an offence under any other enactment relating to money laundering or terrorist financing` IS elem `it is an offence relating to money laundering or terrorist financing` true
        `an offence under any other enactment or under customary law involving deception or dishonesty` IS elem `it is an offence involving deception or dishonesty` true
        `an offence under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey similar to one listed in (i) to (v)` IS elem `it is an offence under foreign law similar to those` true

-- The same for a charity that stood in the general section both when the conduct occurred and when asked, with the Companies Law as its constitutional Law.
GIVEN true IS A LIST OF `A thing true of the conduct`
GIVETH A `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)`
`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` true MEANS
    `a piece of conduct of which` true `is true, with the entity` `entered in the general section` `at the time and` `entered in the general section` `when asked, and the laws` (LIST `the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`)

-- The same for a charity with no constitutional Law (an unincorporated association).
GIVEN true IS A LIST OF `A thing true of the conduct`
GIVETH A `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)`
`conduct of a registered charity with no constitutional Law when these are true:` true MEANS
    `a piece of conduct of which` true `is true, with the entity` `entered in the general section` `at the time and` `entered in the general section` `when asked, and the laws` EMPTY

-- The misconduct question with the standard inputs left at their neutral values: no contravention of the Law reported, not an excepted foreign charity, no notice served.
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
      conduct IS A `Facts about conduct under Article 2(10)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`misconduct on the facts alone, under` interp `of` conduct MEANS
    `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` interp conduct FALSE FALSE EMPTY

`a notice served on the charity` MEANS
    LIST (`Required steps notice` WITH
              `served on` IS `the registered charity`
              `prompted by` IS `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`
              `date served` IS YMD 2024 3 1
              `steps to be taken by` IS NOTHING
              `requires a governor to be suspended, removed or replaced` IS FALSE
              `has been complied with` IS FALSE)

-- (a)(i): a contravention of this Law or of an enactment under it is the standard input IP13.
#ASSERT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` EMPTY) FALSE TRUE EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` EMPTY) FALSE FALSE EMPTY EQUALS FALSE
-- ... even if the facts of the conduct do not say who did it (IP13 is already "the charity or governor").
#ASSERT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` (`conduct of a registered charity with no constitutional Law when these are true:` EMPTY) FALSE TRUE EMPTY
-- ... in the restricted section too.
#ASSERT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` (`a piece of conduct of which` EMPTY `is true, with the entity` `entered in the restricted section` `at the time and` `entered in the restricted section` `when asked, and the laws` EMPTY) FALSE TRUE EMPTY
-- ... but by a registered charity: an entity that was not registered when the conduct occurred is not.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` (`a piece of conduct of which` EMPTY `is true, with the entity` `not on the register` `at the time and` `entered in the general section` `when asked, and the laws` EMPTY) FALSE TRUE EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` (`a piece of conduct of which` EMPTY `is true, with the entity` `an applicant for registration` `at the time and` `an applicant for registration` `when asked, and the laws` EMPTY) FALSE TRUE EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` (`a piece of conduct of which` EMPTY `is true, with the entity` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` `at the time and` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` `when asked, and the laws` EMPTY) FALSE TRUE EMPTY

-- F1.7: the charity was registered in the general section when the conduct occurred and has since been deregistered (the historic section).
`a contravention by a charity since deregistered` MEANS
    `a piece of conduct of which` EMPTY `is true, with the entity` `entered in the general section` `at the time and` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` `when asked, and the laws` EMPTY
-- ... and the converse: not yet registered when the conduct occurred, registered when asked.
`a contravention before the charity was registered` MEANS
    `a piece of conduct of which` EMPTY `is true, with the entity` `an applicant for registration` `at the time and` `entered in the general section` `when asked, and the laws` EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `a contravention by a charity since deregistered` FALSE TRUE EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.7 read the other way` `a contravention by a charity since deregistered` FALSE TRUE EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `a contravention before the charity was registered` FALSE TRUE EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.7 read the other way` `a contravention before the charity was registered` FALSE TRUE EMPTY

-- (a)(ii): the constitution, and the constitutional Law of the charity.
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is by the registered charity or by one of its governors`, `it contravenes the constitution`))
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is by the registered charity or by one of its governors`, `it contravenes the constitutional Law`))
#ASSERT NOT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it contravenes the constitution`))
#ASSERT NOT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it contravenes the constitutional Law`))
-- ... where the definition of "constitutional Law" names none, there is no such Law to contravene; the constitution itself can still be contravened.
#ASSERT NOT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered charity with no constitutional Law when these are true:` (LIST `it is by the registered charity or by one of its governors`, `it contravenes the constitutional Law`))
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered charity with no constitutional Law when these are true:` (LIST `it is by the registered charity or by one of its governors`, `it contravenes the constitution`))
#ASSERT `Art 2(10)(a)(ii) a provision of the constitution or of the constitutional Law of the charity has been contravened` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it contravenes the constitution`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(10)(a)(ii) a provision of the constitution or of the constitutional Law of the charity has been contravened` (`conduct of a registered charity with no constitutional Law when these are true:` (LIST `it contravenes the constitutional Law`))

-- (a)(iii): a required steps notice; there must be one served.
#ASSERT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is by the registered charity or by one of its governors`, `it contravenes a required steps notice`)) FALSE FALSE `a notice served on the charity`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is by the registered charity or by one of its governors`, `it contravenes a required steps notice`)) FALSE FALSE EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` EMPTY) FALSE FALSE `a notice served on the charity`
#ASSERT `Art 2(10)(a)(iii) a provision of a required steps notice has been contravened` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it contravenes a required steps notice`)) `a notice served on the charity`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(10)(a)(iii) a provision of a required steps notice has been contravened` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it contravenes a required steps notice`)) EMPTY

-- (a)(iv): an order of the court under this Law, under an enactment under this Law, under the constitutional Law of the charity, or under an enactment under that Law.
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is by the registered charity or by one of its governors`, `it contravenes a court order under this Law`))
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is by the registered charity or by one of its governors`, `it contravenes a court order under an enactment under this Law`))
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is by the registered charity or by one of its governors`, `it contravenes a court order under the constitutional Law`))
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is by the registered charity or by one of its governors`, `it contravenes a court order under an enactment under the constitutional Law`))
#ASSERT NOT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered charity with no constitutional Law when these are true:` (LIST `it is by the registered charity or by one of its governors`, `it contravenes a court order under the constitutional Law`))
#ASSERT NOT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered charity with no constitutional Law when these are true:` (LIST `it is by the registered charity or by one of its governors`, `it contravenes a court order under an enactment under the constitutional Law`))
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered charity with no constitutional Law when these are true:` (LIST `it is by the registered charity or by one of its governors`, `it contravenes a court order under this Law`))
-- A contravention by someone who is neither the charity nor one of its governors is not within (a).
#ASSERT NOT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it contravenes a court order under this Law`))

-- (b): an offence, by any person, in relation to a registered charity (the favoured reading F1.2: every limb).
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is an offence in relation to the entity`, `it is an offence under the constitutional Law of that charity or other entity`))
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is an offence in relation to the entity`, `it is an offence under the financial services Laws`))
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is an offence in relation to the entity`, `it is an offence under the tax Laws`))
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is an offence in relation to the entity`, `it is an offence relating to money laundering or terrorist financing`))
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is an offence in relation to the entity`, `it is an offence involving deception or dishonesty`))
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is an offence in relation to the entity`, `it is an offence under foreign law similar to those`))
-- ... but not an offence in relation to the charity of a kind none of the six limbs lists.
#ASSERT NOT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is an offence in relation to the entity`))
-- The offence "under the constitutional Law of that charity": a registered charity whose constitutional Law the definition does not name has none.
#ASSERT NOT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered charity with no constitutional Law when these are true:` (LIST `it is an offence in relation to the entity`, `it is an offence under the constitutional Law of that charity or other entity`))
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered charity with no constitutional Law when these are true:` (LIST `it is an offence in relation to the entity`, `it is an offence under the tax Laws`))

-- F1.2, the discriminating case: a governor convicted of an Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961 offence on a personal return unrelated to the charity.
-- Reading A (taken): the offence must be in relation to the charity, so it is not misconduct; reading B: only limb (i) is tied to the charity, so it is.
`a personal tax offence by a governor` MEANS
    `conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is an offence under the tax Laws`)
#ASSERT NOT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` `a personal tax offence by a governor`
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.2 read the other way` `of` `a personal tax offence by a governor`
-- Reading B still ties limb (i) to the charity.
#ASSERT NOT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.2 read the other way` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is an offence under the constitutional Law of that charity or other entity`))
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.2 read the other way` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is an offence in relation to the entity`, `it is an offence under the constitutional Law of that charity or other entity`))
-- Each of limbs (ii) to (vi) on reading B, without the connection.
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.2 read the other way` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is an offence under the financial services Laws`))
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.2 read the other way` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is an offence relating to money laundering or terrorist financing`))
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.2 read the other way` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is an offence involving deception or dishonesty`))
#ASSERT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.2 read the other way` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` (LIST `it is an offence under foreign law similar to those`))
-- ... and nothing at all is still nothing on either reading.
#ASSERT NOT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.2 read the other way` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` EMPTY)

-- (b), the connection: "a registered charity or ... an excepted foreign charity (within the meaning of Article 22) or ... an entity equivalent to a registered charity under the law of a jurisdiction other than Jersey".
`an offence in relation to an entity that is none of those` MEANS
    `a piece of conduct of which` (LIST `it is an offence in relation to the entity`, `it is an offence under the tax Laws`) `is true, with the entity` `not on the register` `at the time and` `not on the register` `when asked, and the laws` EMPTY
`an offence in relation to an equivalent foreign entity` MEANS
    `a piece of conduct of which` (LIST `it is an offence in relation to the entity`, `it is an offence under the tax Laws`, `the entity is equivalent to a registered charity abroad`) `is true, with the entity` `not on the register` `at the time and` `not on the register` `when asked, and the laws` EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `an offence in relation to an entity that is none of those` FALSE FALSE EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `an offence in relation to an entity that is none of those` TRUE FALSE EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `an offence in relation to an equivalent foreign entity` FALSE FALSE EMPTY
-- The offence under the constitutional Law of a foreign entity is its own Law's, an input: no guard from the Jersey definition.
#ASSERT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` (`a piece of conduct of which` (LIST `it is an offence in relation to the entity`, `it is an offence under the constitutional Law of that charity or other entity`, `the entity is equivalent to a registered charity abroad`) `is true, with the entity` `not on the register` `at the time and` `not on the register` `when asked, and the laws` EMPTY) FALSE FALSE EMPTY
-- Reading B ties nothing to the connection for (ii) to (vi): the same offence, in relation to an entity that is none of those, is misconduct.
#ASSERT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.2 read the other way` `an offence in relation to an entity that is none of those` FALSE FALSE EMPTY

-- F1.7 in (b): the offence was in relation to a charity registered when it was committed, deregistered since.
`an offence in relation to a charity since deregistered` MEANS
    `a piece of conduct of which` (LIST `it is an offence in relation to the entity`, `it is an offence under the tax Laws`) `is true, with the entity` `entered in the restricted section` `at the time and` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section` `when asked, and the laws` EMPTY
#ASSERT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `an offence in relation to a charity since deregistered` FALSE FALSE EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.7 read the other way` `an offence in relation to a charity since deregistered` FALSE FALSE EMPTY
-- ... which the entity's being an excepted foreign charity (IP26) would cure, as the Law lists it as a separate connection.
#ASSERT `Art 2(10) the conduct is misconduct` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.7 read the other way` `an offence in relation to a charity since deregistered` TRUE FALSE EMPTY

-- (a) is not (b): a registered charity's contravention of its own constitution is misconduct under (a), and an offence nobody committed in relation to it is not.
#ASSERT NOT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.2 read the other way` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `misconduct on the facts alone, under` `the interpretation of Articles 1 and 2 with F1.7 read the other way` `of` (`conduct of a registered company charity when these are true:` EMPTY)
